    {
        "content": "<p>I asked Claude Opus your question and here is its answer (which I did not verify):</p>\n<hr>\n<p>The culprit is a diamond on <code>SMul ↥H (G ⧸ H)</code>. With <code>set_option pp.explicit true</code>, the two <code>h • x</code>s in your second example use different instances:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>MulAction.mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal G H H</code>, i.e. <code>MulAction.compHom (G ⧸ H) H.subtype</code> (<code>Mathlib/GroupTheory/GroupAction/Quotient.lean</code>), and</li>\n<li><code>Submonoid.instMulActionSubtypeMem</code> applied to <code>MulAction.quotient</code> — the generic \"restrict a <code>MulAction G α</code> along <code>↥H → G</code>\" instance (<code>Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Submonoid/MulAction.lean</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>MulAction.subgroup_smul_def</code> is stated for a general <code>α</code> with <code>[MulAction G α]</code>, so its LHS uses the generic <code>Submonoid</code> instance, which is declared <code>(priority := low)</code>; at <code>α := G ⧸ H</code> elaboration instead picks the bespoke <code>mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</code>. The two are defeq, but only by unfolding, and <code>rw</code>'s keyed matching unfolds instances at reducible transparency only — hence \"did not find an occurrence\" in your third example. The pattern genuinely is absent, syntactically.</p>\n<p>In the <code>←</code> direction the <em>right</em>-hand side <code>↑h • x</code> matches fine (that instance argument is just a metavariable to be assigned from the target), and the rewrite then installs the lemma's own LHS, carrying the <code>Submonoid</code> instance with it. So your goal is really <code>h •[compHom] x = h •[Submonoid] x</code>, which prints as <code>h • x = h • x</code>. <code>rw</code> finishes by trying <code>with_reducible rfl</code>, which fails; your <code>rfl</code> on the next line uses default transparency and succeeds. <code>simp [MulAction.subgroup_smul_def]</code> reports \"simp made no progress\" on the original goal for the same reason, whereas <code>exact MulAction.subgroup_smul_def h x</code> works because <code>exact</code> unifies at default transparency.</p>\n<p>Two workarounds:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- to rewrite inside a bigger goal</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hP</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Arguably this is a mathlib wart rather than something you should have to work around. <code>MulAction.left_quotientAction : QuotientAction G H</code> always fires, so <code>MulAction G (G ⧸ H)</code> is always available, and the low-priority <code>Submonoid</code> instance then gives <code>MulAction ↥I (G ⧸ H)</code> anyway — so <code>mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</code> looks redundant, and its only effect here is to outrank the generic instance and break <code>subgroup_smul_def</code>. Does anyone know whether it is load-bearing, or could it just be removed?</p>",
        "id": 620440416,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1788208432
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's perhaps a better explanation:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Group</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subgroup_smul_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subgroup_smul_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instMulActionSubtypeMem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instSMulSubtypeMem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compHom</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- goal is SMul.comp.smul ⇑H.subtype = fun m a =&gt; ↑m • a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38968\">#38968</a> is relevant here</p>",
