    {
        "content": "<p>Even with that PR merged, we're still in trouble with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subgroup_smul_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instMulActionSubtypeMem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instSMulSubtypeMem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compHom</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SMul</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">comp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">smul</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- goal is `H.subtype n • a = ↑n • a`</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_reducible_and_instances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which requires us to made <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subgroup.subtype#doc\">docs#Subgroup.subtype</a> instance-reducible</p>",
        "id": 620456553,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788212605
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(in general the pattern here seems to be that _every_ bundled morphism needs to be instance reducible, which starts to suggest that maybe we should have instance-reducibility as the default...)</p>",
        "id": 620456713,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788212650
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"110038\">Kevin Buzzard</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/How.20does.20.60MulAction.2Esubgroup_smul_def.60.20work.20exactly.3F/near/620440416\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I asked Claude Opus your question and here is its answer (which I did not verify):<br>\n<code>MulAction.left_quotientAction : QuotientAction G H</code> always fires, so <code>MulAction G (G ⧸ H)</code> is always available, and the low-priority <code>Submonoid</code> instance then gives <code>MulAction ↥I (G ⧸ H)</code> anyway — so <code>mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</code> looks redundant. </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed, Claude Opus is right that<code>mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</code> is redundant, as I verified <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43276\">#43276</a>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">--succeed</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">to_additive</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mulLeftCosetsCompSubtypeVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">subtype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">I</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 620497388,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1788226859
    }
